WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.602
-As he continues to deal
with the aftermath

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:05.371
of his disastrous response
to the humanitarian crisis

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.207
in Puerto Rico,
President Trump is now also

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.109
dealing with
an internal crisis --

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.578
a simmering feud
with the Secretary of State.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.481
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.750 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.552
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.422
After his tour of Puerto Rico,
where he chided Puerto Ricans

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.157
for throwing the budget
out of whack

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.359
and tossed paper towels
into the crowd

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.495
like he was
at the free-throw line,

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:32.431
Trump did what he always does --
bragged about his performance

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:35.802
and made up a bizarre
and completely unnecessary lie

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.505
about how unprecedented
his trip was.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.240
He told reporters
on<i> Air Force One...</i>

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.916
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.089
You think this is the first time
a sitting President

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.425
has visited hurricane victims?

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.195
This isn't even the first time
<i> you've</i> done it!

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.629
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.233
You were just in Texas
and Florida a few weeks ago.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:11.271
Remember? Oh, no!
You<i> don't</i> remember, do you?

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.605
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.206
This is turning
into "50 First Dates,"

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.042
but for hurricanes.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.177
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:21.047
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.215
In a way, though...

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.484
In a way, though,
Trump is right.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.019
This is the first time
a sitting President

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:28.888
has embarrassed himself
this much

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.324
while trying to comfort the
victims of a natural disaster.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.959
For example, after he threw
supplies at hurricane victims,

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:36.662
the crowd literally
had to tell him to stop.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.031
According to
the "Washington Post"...

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.942
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.445
My God.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:56.215
Our President had to be told not
to throw cans of chicken...

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.950
[ Laughter ]
...at hurricane victims.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.686
I wouldn't be surprised if he
only built Trump Tower

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.623
so he could drop pennies
off the roof.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.024
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.428
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:10.864
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:11.998
Of all...

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.233
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.536
Of all Trump's missteps in
Puerto Rico, there's one that is

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.572
perhaps the most embarrassing
and also the most revealing.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.607
At the church where supplies
were being handed out,

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.309
he encountered a church member

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.645
giving out
water purification tablets.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.547
Basically, these tablets
turn dirty water

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.150
into clean drinking water,
and not only could Trump

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.386
not believe it worked,
he couldn't believe

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.120
they were giving it away
for free.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.590
Here's how that exchange went,
according to the "Post"...

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.883
Trump genuinely cannot
contemplate doing something

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.951
out of the goodness
of your heart.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:08.688
He just assumes it must be
a scam.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.689
[ Imitating Trump ] So you give
them the dirty water,

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.190
but you say it's clean?

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.025
[ Normal voice ]
No, it's clean.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:14.327
[ Imitating Trump ]
Oh, so you clean the water,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.062
but then you sell it
for double the price?

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.531
[ Normal voice ]
No, we give it away for free.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.932
[ Imitating Trump ]
Oh, I get it. So while they're

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.066
drinking the water,
you go around

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.769
and steal all their wallets?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.005
[ Normal voice ] But this --
this is yet another reminder

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.874
to the evangelicals
who support Trump.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:31.610
He doesn't understand church.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.080
[ Imitating Trump ]
What's Jesus' cut, 20%?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.182
That's very good.
That's a lot of cans of chicken.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.884
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.985
[ Normal voice ] But after
embarrassing himself,

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.319
insulting the people
of Puerto Rico,

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.821
and repeatedly bringing up
the financial cost

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.856
of the recovery,
Trump out of nowhere

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.626
seemed to throw Puerto Rico
a potential lifeline.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.294
Right now the government
of Puerto Rico is dealing

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.397
with an economic crisis
and billions of dollars in debt

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.866
bought up by hedge funds
and other Wall Street firms

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.702
who have blocked any attempt to
allow Puerto Rico

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.138
to restructure its debt
or declare bankruptcy.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.007
But as Trump was leaving
the island on Tuesday,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.208
he seemed to suggest
he might support

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.711
forgiving Puerto Rico's debt
completely.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:06.945
-We're going to work
something out.

00:04:06.945 --> 00:04:09.081
We have to look at
their whole debt structure.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.850
You know, they owe
a lot of money

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.785
to your friends on Wall Street,
and we're going to have to

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.154
wipe that out.
That's gonna have to be, uh,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.555
you know, you can say goodbye
to that.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:17.824
I don't know if it's
Goldman Sachs,

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.859
but whoever it is,
you can wave goodbye to that.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.561
-Well, that would be easy.
I've been waving goodbye

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.697
to things since
you became President.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:28.434
Bye, Constitution!
Bye, good night's sleep!

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.770
Bye, half the people I know
on Facebook!

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.005
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.508
But forgiving
Puerto Rico's debt

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.309
would be a truly
transformative step.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:39.345
It would go a long way to
alleviating the suffering

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.515
of Puerto Ricans and make up for
many of Trump's missteps

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.316
in handling the crisis,
so naturally,

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:45.951
his budget director,
Mick Mulvaney,

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.653
went on TV the next morning
to tell people,

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.256
"Don't listen to the President."

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.792
-The President seemed to
suggest that he is open

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:56.162
to wiping out
the Puerto Rican debt.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.965
Is that to be taken seriously
on its face?

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.334
-I wouldn't take it word
for word with that --

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.571
-Agreed. No one should ever take
Trump word for word.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.140
It's far more fun to take
his words

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.777
and then put them in an order
that you find interesting.

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:14.614
-I have Wall Street friends.
I have a lot of money.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.016
I have butt hole. I have
butt hole. I have butt hole.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.551
Goodbye.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.319
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:21.654
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Very proud of that.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:22.989
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.224
Of course, the President isn't
content to botch

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.192
just one crisis, which is why
he's in the process

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:29.362
of botching another --
North Korea's nuclear program.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.897
The international community has
been desperately pursuing

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:34.867
every diplomatic angle to avoid
what would certainly be

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:37.503
a catastrophic war,
and Trump's own government

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:38.938
has been working with
the U.N. Security Council,

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.806
China, and even through
back channels

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.542
of North Korea itself to resolve
the conflict peacefully.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.045
So once again, Trump threw
all that out the window

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:48.881
when he tweeted out of nowhere
over the weekend...

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.127
So all the careful diplomacy
and bargaining and angling

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:02.661
just goes out the window
with one tweet.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:05.398
It's like everyone is playing
an intense game of Jenga,

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:08.000
and Trump is the rambunctious
golden retriever

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.702
barging through the doggy door.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.702 --> 00:06:12.505
Also, I wouldn't be too
concerned

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.508
that Rex Tillerson is expending
a lot of energy.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.543
He looks like the guy
sitting in a rocking chair

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.612
outside the corner store
who says...

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.180
[ Elderly Southern voice ]
Storm's a-comin'. I can feel it

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.383
in my knees.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:27.653
[ Applause ]

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:31.457
[ Normal voice ] So Trump
has once again undercut

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.159
the diplomatic efforts
of the Secretary of State,

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.660
which has happened
so many times,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.896
that Tillerson apparently
threatened to resign

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.263
over the summer,

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:40.466
according to a report yesterday
from NBC News.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.435
But the fact that Tillerson
threatened to resign

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:44.203
is not the most damning part
of the story.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:45.604
That, of course, had to do

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:48.274
with what Tillerson called Trump
behind his back.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.608
-At a meeting at the Pentagon

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:50.976
with the President's
National Security team,

00:06:50.976 --> 00:06:53.112
there were cabinet officials,
White House officials.

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:55.848
The President attended.
He left.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:58.317
The group was gathering. There
were a number of people around,

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:01.454
and the Secretary called
the President a moron.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:04.857
Wow. And Tillerson has that
great Texas accent,

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:07.159
so you know
he really stretched it out.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:10.363
[ Southern accent ]
That guy is a<i> more-ron.</i>

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:11.998
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.599
[ Normal voice ] Now, obviously,
this story was based

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:16.502
on anonymous sources, and
the State Department denied it,

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.571
which is why MSNBC
did their own reporting

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.139
on exactly what Tillerson said

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:23.743
and issued an important
clarification later that day.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:26.178
-My source didn't just say
that he called him a moron.

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:28.147
He said "an effing moron."

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.048
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:33.852
-This story keeps
getting better and better.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.955
Seriously, I can't wait
for the next update.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:39.024
Oh, here it is right here.
"Sources have further clarified

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:41.727
"that Tillerson called Trump
a 'straight up nose-pickin'

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.361
"'mouth-breathin',
missed-a-belt-loop...

00:07:43.361 --> 00:07:44.931
[bleep]<i> more-on.'"</i>

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:47.500
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.703
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.038
Tillerson, of course, was forced
to issue a statement

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:55.107
at a hastily arranged
press conference yesterday,

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:57.976
where he took the extraordinary
step of trying to assure

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.878
the American people
that the President is not,

00:07:59.878 --> 00:08:01.680
in fact, a moron.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.982
-Let me tell you what I've
learned about this President,

00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:07.819
whom I did not know before
taking this office.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:10.189
He loves his country.

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:13.659
He puts Americans
and America first.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:14.927
He's smart...

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.763
-Man, to think a guy's a moron
and then be forced

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.798
to publicly say he's smart.

00:08:19.798 --> 00:08:21.333
I guess when your name is Rex,

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.269
you're gonna be good
at rolling over.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.671
[ Laughter ]
Good boy, Rex! Good boy!

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.573
[ Applause ]
Oh, stay away from the Jenga!

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:30.675
[ Applause ]
Now, yesterday, while he was

00:08:30.675 --> 00:08:33.178
in Las Vegas, Trump was asked
about the Tillerson story

00:08:33.178 --> 00:08:35.814
in his comments afterwards
and could not stop himself

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:37.183
from attacking the media.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.817
Watch as he keeps saying
"thank you"

00:08:38.817 --> 00:08:42.722
as if to stop talking
and then continues to ramble.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.757
-Yeah, I'm very honored by
his comments. It was fake news.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.992
It was a totally phony story.
Thank you very much.

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.261
It was made up.
It was made up by NBC.

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:49.595
They just made it up.
Thank you all.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:52.064
-Do you have confidence in him?
-Thank you.

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:54.700
-Total confidence in Rex.
I have total confidence.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.602
Thank you very much, everybody.
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:59.604
-You can almost see the angel
and devil on his shoulders

00:08:59.604 --> 00:09:00.806
wrestling for control.

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.174
[ Devilish voice ]
Say it was fake news!

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:03.742
[ High-pitched voice ]
No, say thank you and leave.

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:05.177
[ Devilish voice ]
Call it a phony story!

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:06.978
[ High-pitched voice ] Walk away
and don't throw chicken cans!

00:09:06.978 --> 00:09:08.347
[ Devilish voice ]
Throw the chicken! Throw it!

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:09.448
[ High-pitched voice ] No,
throw the paper towels

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.983
but not the chicken!

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.318
[ Devilish voice ]
Throw the chicken,

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.286
but wrap it in paper towels
so they think it's soft!

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:17.890
[ Cheers and applause,
whistles ]

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.825
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:22.461
We're in a truly extraordinary
situation where the President

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:24.763
is fighting with
his own Secretary of State,

00:09:24.763 --> 00:09:27.033
as he faces multiple
foreign policy challenges.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:30.035
In fact, cabinet officials are
apparently now so concerned

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:32.972
about the President's volatility
that several of them have forged

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:36.375
an agreement to quit if Trump
tries to fire one of them...

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:51.023
Jesus, so three cabinet
officials have to ban together

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:52.758
to deal with
their out-of-control boss.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:56.095
They're treating him like he's
Dabney Coleman in "9 to 5."

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:58.296
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.296 --> 00:10:00.032
And before you say that was
a dated reference,

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:03.536
they were all at the Emmys!
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:04.970
So this is the situation
we're in.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.807
Cabinet officials are forming
suicide pacts

00:10:07.807 --> 00:10:09.408
to protect each other
from the President.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:12.812
The President is volatile,
unstable, incompetent.

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:14.680
In other words...
-A moron.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.750
-No, that's not it.
-An effing moron.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.152
-Yeah, that's it.
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.654 line:0%
♪♪

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:23.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

